From 1d798bc00b03ec81fd4997b5083b4de658edd50a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 12:30:22 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] Keep a borrowed second Pluto chain in step with the
 first, and switch an amplifier from a GPO pin (#525)

The receive thread can now commit a 2R2T buffer to both chains' rings or to
neither, recording where chain 1 starts in chain 0's count, so
PlutoRx::rx_read_paired hands over the two chains' samples of the same
instants. PlutoRig::aux_rx borrows chain 1 that way.

Phy::setup_pa_switch puts one GPO pin in the AD9361's manual mode at the
requested level before the initialise, and Phy::set_pa flips it live through
the driver's gpo_set entry. It works in FDD, and is refused with a note beside
a PTT pair, which needs the same pins slaved. Loopback tests cover pairing,
the switch, and the refusal.
---
