Subject: [PATCH 5/6] PlutoSDR PureSignal: look back a second for the feedback,
 and find the delay afresh each over (#525)

On a PlutoSky R2 over Ethernet PureSignal never locked: the transmission
comes back on RX2 a few hundred milliseconds after it was predistorted
(host ring, DMA buffers both ways, the network twice), well past the tenth
of a second PureSignal::new keeps. PureSignal::with_history takes a longer
history, and while unlocked the search now runs eight times a second rather
than on every block, so the longer history costs nothing extra. The Pluto
uses one second, and unlocks at each key-up so the two sample counts the
delay is measured between start together. A test covers a delay the default
history cannot reach.
