From 2d97ffe5ca9f37010a27e07434e06a394b7f7246 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yankneck696 <yankneck696@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 17:14:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] Two-tone test signal on TUNE, and keep up with fast
 receivers through a full-duplex over (#525)

A 2T chip beside TUNE transmits 700 Hz and 1900 Hz together at the tune
level until clicked again, like the Tone button other SDR programs have:
the signal amplifier linearity is judged with, and the one PureSignal learns
from, since a steady carrier has a single amplitude. TxState gains two_tone
and Command gains SetTuneTwoTone; wire protocol v175. Keying and level are
TUNE's own, so every guard on TUNE applies.

During a full-duplex over the engine read one 16384-sample block per 10 ms
tick, a 1.64 Msps ceiling: a 2.083 Msps PlutoSDR dropped a fifth of its
receive, which is also PureSignal's feedback. It now takes up to four blocks
a tick when that many are already waiting, still never waiting for more.
